NAME
    swarm-core - run coding agents in Docker over a shared Git repository

SYNOPSIS
    bin/launch.sh start [--dashboard]
    bin/launch.sh wait
    bin/launch.sh interactive NAME
    bin/launch.sh cleanup

DESCRIPTION
    Each agent runs in a container of its own and pushes to one bare
    repository; there is no orchestrator.  swarm.json, in the root of
    the repository to work on, names the agents.

    start launches the agents.  wait post-processes and harvests their
    work into the checkout.  interactive opens a human-guided session.
    cleanup deletes the engagement and keeps recovery refs.

PREREQUISITES
    Docker, Bash 5, Git, jq, bc, perl, flock, tput, and credentials for
    a driver.

DRIVERS
    claude-code (default), pi, codex-cli, gemini-cli.

SEE ALSO
    USAGE for configuration, commands, authentication and the control
    interface.  NEWS for the changes in each release.

LICENSE
    AGPL-3.0, see COPYING.
